<title>CHILE: Chilean forex reserves rise to $17.6 billion.</title>
<headline>Chilean forex reserves rise to $17.6 billion.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's foreign reserves climbed $502 million last month to $17.598 billion at June 30, the Central Bank reported.</p>
<p>Reserves at the end of 1996 stood at $15.474 billion and $14.805 billion at the end of 1995, the bank said in its twice-monthly report on economic indicators.</p>
<p>((-- Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
